mapledmaaddr (#528) -- KILL TABLE 3, PRETABLE, written 2026-09-12 BEFORE the table runs.  Post-table notes go in a
SEPARATE file (POSTTABLE.out), so this file's mtime stays the order evidence.

WHY A TABLE 3.  The §F2 adjudication pass (_scratchpad/panel_20260912_143959_mapleadjud, 7/7 scriptable seats
answered) named survivors of the 29-row instrument that kill table 2 measured:
    M_ALIAS01 / M_ALIAS02  `switch (relative_addr & ~0x01ULL)' / `& ~0x02ULL' (kimi, CLI and ollama).  A mov.b at 0x05
                     and a mov.w at 0x06 reach the device (they are aligned for their width), so the CONTRACT's
                     "0x05/0x06 ... an SH4 address error before the device" was TRUE ONLY FOR mov.l -- an L4 wrong
                     record in the unshipped header, now corrected.
    M_CASE00         `case 0x00:' stacked on the DMAADDR label (codex).  0x00 was never read.
    M_HEXDIAG        `fatal("0x%08x\n", (unsigned)d->dmaaddr);' (codex).  The quiet grammar admits a bare hex line
                     because a `print' answer IS one; a grammar is a whitelist of SHAPES and cannot see a diagnostic
                     that takes a legal shape.
    M_JOINTDECLINE   `} else if (!d->enable || (d->dmaaddr & 0x1f)) {' (codex): declines only in the joint cell,
                     enabled AND aligned; `read aligned' and `read enabled' each hold only one half.
    M_SIBLING        the read arm also writes `d->enable = 1;' (kimi: sibling-state side effects).  `other 0x14' read
                     ENABLE, but no DMAADDR read preceded it in that session.
    M_LEN1           a silent exit under `len == 1' (kimi).  `read width16' pins len 2 only.
The detector is UNSHIPPED, so every repair is L1 construction.  The FIX IS UNCHANGED (no seat disputed it).

CHANGES -- 35 rows, MEASURED 35/35 CONTROL=OK on the fixed build/ binary before this block (cmp CLEAN, binary FRESH):
_scratchpad/maple_base35.out, copied here as BASE_prelaunch.out.
  * noise(t, cmds): besides any line outside the quiet grammar, a READ session is noisy if any grammar line CLASS
    (bare hex / `put' confirmation / stepped disassembly) has a count different from what its commands owe: one hex
    line per `rN=' / `pc=' / `print', one confirmation per `put', one disassembly line per stepped instruction.
    Measured on the fixed build: every one of the twelve read sessions balances (read silent 0/12), so the accounting
    is exact, not approximate.  CONSEQUENCE FOR EVERY EXIT LEG: a session that dies owes lines it never prints, so
    `read silent' now reds deterministically on ANY dead read session.  That replaces table 2's timing-dependent
    dead-pty `quit' echo (M_BIT30's miss) with a certainty.
  * `other pre read': a DMAADDR read FIRST in the others session (register r9), so a sibling write shows at 0x14/0x80.
  * `alias 0x00' (mov.l), `alias 0x05' (mov.b), `alias 0x06' (mov.w), in the alias session (NOT silence-counted).
  * `read width8' (mov.b at 0x04: low byte 0x45), in the width16 session (width16 now via load32(op=LD_W)).
  * `read joint': in the enabled session, after `read enabled', an aligned value written and read.
  Twelve read sessions, unchanged in number: val_a, val_b, others, width, survive, initial, four, all ones, aligned,
  enabled, triple, replace.

ROW-LIST DIFF against table 2's PRETABLE (the carried-forward check): every table-2 row is still present by name; the
table-2 PRETABLE prescribed no row that is absent here.

INSTRUMENT: maple_dmaaddr_probe.FROZEN3.py, copied from regress/ at launch.  BASELINE: SEC (the fix).  HEAD:
dev_dreamcast_maple.HEAD.c (cmp-identical to `git show HEAD:').  MUTATOR: mut_maple3.py -- table 2's legs verbatim
plus the seven above.  Each new leg was dry-run against SEC and its diff read before this block (one hunk each).

PREDICTIONS (score / 35; failing rows).  HEAD's value set is 23 rows: val_a, val_b, other pre read + the six `other'
rows (the session now reads DMAADDR first, so it dies there), width16, width8, marker survive, exit status, initial
zero, read four, read all ones, read aligned, read enabled, read joint, double 1, double 2, reread 3, write replace.
  BASE            35/35 CONTROL=OK
  HEAD            11/35  the 23 value rows + read silent (12/12) = 24 failing; controls and the 7 alias rows pass
  M_KEEPFATAL     34/35  read silent alone
  M_REWORD        34/35  read silent alone
  M_LATCHED       34/35  read silent alone (once per process = once per session)
  M_TOKENFREE     34/35  read silent alone
  M_EXITONLY      11/35  as HEAD (read silent by the deficit, no diagnostic needed)
  M_RET0          19/35  val_a, val_b, pre read, width16, width8, initial zero, four, all ones, aligned, enabled,
                         joint, d1, d2, reread 3, replace (15 poisoned) + read silent (memory_rw's failed-access
                         line) = 16; marker survive and exit status pass, the six `other' rows pass
  M_DECLINE       21/35  val_a, val_b, pre read, width16, width8, four, all ones, aligned, enabled, joint, d1, d2,
                         reread 3, replace (14); initial zero passes
  M_HOIST         25/35  other 0x10, 0x8c, 0xe8 + all seven alias rows (0x05 -> 0x45, 0x06 -> 0x2345, the rest the
                         field) = 10
  M_READCLEAR     32/35  double read 2, reread 3, read width8 (width16's read cleared it)
  M_EQ4           33/35  read four + read silent
  M_BIT30         33/35  read all ones + read silent (no other written value sets bit 30)
  M_ZEROEXIT      31/35  initial zero, marker survive, exit status + read silent
  M_MASKLOW       23/35  val_a, val_b, pre read, width16, width8, four, all ones, enabled, d1, d2, reread 3, replace
                         (12); aligned, joint, initial zero pass
  M_ALIAS08       33/35  alias 0x0c + read silent (0x8c -> 0x84 and 0xe8 -> 0xe0 hit the default arm in `others')
  M_ALIAS20       33/35  alias 0x24 + read silent (0xe8 -> 0xc8)
  M_ALIAS40       33/35  alias 0x44 + read silent (0xe8 -> 0xa8)
  M_AND4          27/35  other 0x14, other 0x8c, alias 0x0c/0x24/0x44/0x84, alias 0x05, alias 0x06 (8); 0x00 and
                         0xe8 have bit 2 clear; redirected reads are quiet
  M_LEN           32/35  width16, width8 (the session died at width16) + read silent
  M_ALIGNDECLINE  33/35  read aligned, read joint (initial zero declines to 0 and still passes)
  M_ENDECLINE     33/35  read enabled, read joint
  M_ALIGNEXIT     32/35  read aligned, read joint + read silent
  M_ENEXIT        32/35  read enabled, read joint + read silent
  M_THIRDREAD     33/35  reread 3 + read silent (no other session reads DMAADDR three times: others 1, width 2,
                         enabled 2)
  M_ALIAS01       34/35  alias 0x05 alone (every case label is even)
  M_ALIAS02       34/35  alias 0x06 alone (0x05 & ~2 == 0x05 stays in the default arm)
  M_CASE00        34/35  alias 0x00 alone
  M_HEXDIAG       34/35  read silent alone -- THE LEG THAT TESTS THE COUNT ACCOUNTING.  Checked before writing this:
                         table 2's diagnostics landed on their OWN line under stepping (probe_M_KEEPFATAL.raw /
                         probe_M_TOKENFREE.raw / probe_M_RET0.raw `noise:' lines are the whole diagnostic), so the hex
                         line is a surplus hex line, not a suffix on the disassembly line
  M_JOINTDECLINE  34/35  read joint alone
  M_SIBLING       34/35  other 0x14 alone (reads 1)
  M_LEN1          33/35  read width8 + read silent

CHECKS.
  SIBLING PARITY -- the arm's nearest sibling is MAPLE_ENABLE's read (0x14), which answers its field quietly; the fix
    makes 0x04 do the same.  No asymmetry owed.
  CLAIM -> ROW -- every CONTRACT sentence names its row: the count accounting (read silent, M_HEXDIAG); sub-word
    aliases (alias 0x05, alias 0x06); 0x00 (alias 0x00); joint (read joint); sibling writes (other pre read then other
    0x14 / 0x80); 8-bit access (read width8).  The NOT-COVERED list carries the rest by class, each clause (e).
  GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- the dominating predicates are `relative_addr' (the switch) and `writeflag'; the guarded
    body reads `d->dmaaddr' only.  `d->enable' and the alignment bits are read by maple_do_dma_xfer(), outside the
    enclosing function -- outside DEPENDS-ON's BOUND; their rows are L1.
  CHANNEL -- each new row: alias 0x05 / M_ALIAS01, VALUE (0 vs 0x45); alias 0x06 / M_ALIAS02, VALUE (0 vs 0x2345);
    alias 0x00 / M_CASE00, VALUE (0 vs the field); read silent / M_HEXDIAG, the hex-line COUNT (one surplus per read);
    read joint / M_JOINTDECLINE, VALUE (the aligned value vs 0); other 0x14 / M_SIBLING, VALUE (0 vs 1), made
    observable only by `other pre read' preceding it; read width8 / M_LEN1, VALUE (0x45 vs absent) and the deficit.
    Every channel varies under its named mutant by construction.
